","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T20:18:48-07:00","id":1111962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1111949#post1111949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Closest to that I've heard was that Chapter One was moved around, with <b>Courts being shoved in as the Y splat instead of Seemings (which were the Y splat in the preview of the completed chapter one).</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That is still not how Y-splats work and this is still not a change from 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T20:23:36-07:00","id":1111963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1111962#post1111962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is still not how Y-splats work and this is still not a change from 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was the splat which the character gets through their agency, it was the Y half to the splat chapter, the splat changelings can change. It's more like the Hunger Y-splat than it is the Covenant Y-splat, but it makes sense to consider it the Y splat of Dave's changeling. But it doesn't really matter whether people consider it a Y-splat or not... I was talking about how the only change we Knew of to that section of the book rather than speculation, was that Courts were being put back in the Splat chapter (which would definitely make them the Y splat).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 07-05-2017, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T05:09:21-07:00","id":1112055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1111949#post1111949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are you getting that from? I don't remember that ever being said.<br /> <br /> Closest to that I've heard was that Chapter One was moved around, with Courts being shoved in as the Y splat instead of Seemings (which were the Y splat in the preview of the completed chapter one).<br /> <br /> Edit: Nevermind, seen the preview now....<br /> <br /> Well that sucks. The Dave's seeming/kith change was amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes his Seeming/Kith change was good, great even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T06:11:41-07:00","id":1112072,"title":"","content":"It made making non-european changelings so much easier than 1e's horrible system, only reason I can see for them them doing it is to reduce pagecount.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T07:20:41-07:00","id":1112092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112072#post1112072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It made making non-european changelings so much easier than 1e's horrible system, only reason I can see for them them doing it is to reduce pagecount.</div> </div> </div> </div> That is very possible, but I doubt that they reduced the total page count, so the question is what did they do with the extra space (aside from adding the indepth Seasonal Courts, which are interesting, but if that is why then that is simply not a trade off that is worth what was lost).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 07-06-2017, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T08:18:46-07:00","id":1112113,"title":"","content":"I'm very glad that the Seemings are going back to what we had in first edition. While the write up for Darklings in Hill's version made me finally like that seeming (and a lot at that), for me, as a whole, they didn't make much sense thematically, or by the rules that had been put out there. Perhaps it was personal taste, perhaps it was 'It's what I learned the first time, and I'm comfortable with that), I'm not sure, but I still liked it more.<br /> <br /> I like this take on True Fae as well. I think it will allow better stories to be told with them. And they're just as scary as before, but much easier to include in a game; and not with a big battle to fight them off, but rather manipulation of rules, and trickery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T09:31:45-07:00","id":1112153,"title":"","content":"It might not be going back. The material isn't flat out saying one way or another; it could be interpretted either way. Personally, I'm leaning towards keeing David's way - the section of Grandmother, Grandmother that hints that Gentry might shape Seemings could just as easily be interpreted to mean that the Bossy Child naturally becomes a Fairest when they try to escape, because being bossy resonates with how the Fairest escape. And so on. <br /> <br /> This could all be just people reading into things that aren't really there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T09:44:00-07:00","id":1112160,"title":"","content":"i'm happy with the changes that the new developers have been making with second edition. while i liked a lot of what david hill developed, the game was so drastically different from 1e as to be a different product entirely. not a bad game, mind you. jus diff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T10:14:43-07:00","id":1112176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112153#post1112153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might not be going back. The material isn't flat out saying one way or another; it could be interpretted either way. Personally, I'm leaning towards keeing David's way - the section of Grandmother, Grandmother that hints that Gentry might shape Seemings could just as easily be interpreted to mean that the Bossy Child naturally becomes a Fairest when they try to escape, because being bossy resonates with how the Fairest escape. And so on. <br /> <br /> This could all be just people reading into things that aren't really there.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wish Rose or Meghan would provide clarity on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T10:16:48-07:00","id":1112177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112176#post1112176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wish Rose or Meghan would provide clarity on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rose did explain it a few minutes ago, it's on the the true fae thread i made","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T10:21:56-07:00","id":1112181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112177#post1112177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rose did explain it a few minutes ago, it's on the the true fae thread i made</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T10:29:40-07:00","id":1112192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1111519#post1111519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I'm excited for is that the Kiths are no longer restricted to a specific Seeming in 2E, but rather your Seeming now has subtle influences as to how you might embody your Kith.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1111922#post1111922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That might not be true anymore, it, appears Seemings and Kiths have reverted to something more akin to 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kiths encompass multiple seemings. Each kith has example interpretations for at least two seemings. Here's an example: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chapter 1</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Nightsinger</b></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;Thank you, you've been a lovely audience. If you'll notice the jar on my lovely accompanist's piano, I accept cash gifts as a sign of your appreciation. Please don\u2019t make the mistake of throwing your platinum card in \u2013 that is, unless you're prepared to deal with the consequences.&quot;</i></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Song is an art almost as old as humanity itself, and something the True Fae are utterly fascinated by. While they can replicate melodic noises and sing songs taught to them by their human slaves, the Gentry are creatively sterile and cannot create songs of their own. Nightsingers are the Kith who actually produce the magical songs the creatures in fairy tales teach heroes or children.<br /> <br /> Nightsingers were almost uniformly some sort of creative before they were stolen away to Faerie. It's not just singers or writers who become this Kith either. While it might seem odd for a sculptor or an oil painter to become a Nightsinger, it's really just a matter of learning to sculpt or paint with words and pledges the same way one might sculpt bronze or paint on a canvas. This is not to say the process is easy. The True Fae have odd and exacting ideas about what makes a good song, so a changeling who produces a less-than-satisfactory piece runs the risk of severe retribution.<br /> <br /> This is a dangerous position to take as a True Fae. Most Nightsingers escape while their Keepers are in the throes of exquisite agony from a song sad enough to make a stone weep, or doubled over in laughter from a bawdy take on a solemn hymn. Some become their song and float straight out the door, carried by the notes they're singing. Stranger things have happened in Arcadia.Nightsingers find that, once they've escaped, their songs hold less power on Earth than they did in Arcadia. They can no longer achieve the myriad of world-bending effects in the solid, consistent mortal world that they could in a realm built entirely of dreams and magic. This, however, does not mean that they're powerless \u2013 far from it. Their ability to completely enthrall others with their song is quietly feared by other Lost.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Fairest:</b> </i>This almond-eyed torch singer will have you opening both your heart and your wallet to her in under an hour. She has no dearth of admirers, but she always goes home alone. Some call her frigid, some call her prudish, but they're always back for more.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Wizened: </i></b>He's not much to look at \u2013 skeletons have more meat on their bones. His wiry black hair sticks out in all the wrong places. But when he opens his mouth to sing, the rafters quake with his baritone and there is not a dry eye in the room by the end of it. He rarely opens his mouth to do anything else.<br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing: </b>When the Nightsinger uses Expression to sing or compose a piece of music, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Siren Song:</b> </i>Spend a point of Glamour and roll Presence + Expression + Wyrd as an instant action to perform, contested by anyone who hears the Nightsinger\u2019s unearthly song with Composure + Supernatural Tolerance. Anyone who fails gains the Swooned Condition (p. XX) and is rooted to the spot for as long as she continues to sing. Any attempt to jar the victim out of it, short of an opposing power or physically attacking or removing them, will fail.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 07-06-2017, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T10:31:13-07:00","id":1112194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112192#post1112192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Kiths encompass multiple seemings. Each kith has example interpretations for at least two seemings. Here's an example:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Oh, good! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T10:35:12-07:00","id":1112197,"title":"","content":"Kiths, at least, seem to be nearly the same format. Though, this is a pretty different power for the kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-06-2017, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T10:59:26-07:00","id":1112215,"title":"","content":"Glad to see the gap between Kith and Seeming remains. It really helped isolate Seemings to allow for the focus on them being narrative roles. I looked at the Seeming drafts again. There is nothing in 1001 Stories that invalidates anything in the draft version. The only change that can be legitimately intuited from the True Fae text is that Seemings no longer have Curses and the Blessing has nothing to do with Clarity. I am amazed that the one change that was clearly made doesn't get mentioned by anyone. Perhaps it went unnoticed or, like me, people don't care. Still, the thread is about what we know. We know Blessings aren't free Clarity sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T11:20:56-07:00","id":1112232,"title":"","content":"Hrm. I quite liked that. Still, hoping Clarity is the same sliding, XP-less scale it was before.<br /> <br /> Still, something that was mentioned on the other thread is that Seeming is still agency-it just wasn't <i>supposed </i>to be, when assigned by your Keeper. An example is a living thunderstorm Elemental who traps her Keeper in a deluge and blows away the walls of his domain. She's an expert disaster relief specialist, now.<br /> <br /> Also, Keepers do not have Clarity-this means it's literally impossible for them to be aware of things outside of their web of Contracts, and they are always attempting to twist reality to fit their whims than changing to fit the world (or even acknowledging that the world has a separate existence then their whims). They can also only regain Willpower via Aspiration, they don't have Anchors like Virtue or Vice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T11:41:25-07:00","id":1112248,"title":"","content":"The sliding Clarity worked for me but I don't know the specific Blessing and Curses would work out well in play. I didn't try. I wasn't invested in them. As long as Blessings are not worse in the end, I have no complaint about the change.<br /> <br /> My take on Seemings was they were a role. They solidified due to a choice and with that choice were consequences and the prelude leading up to the choice, The Escape. I always saw it as a process and evolution that didn't complete until the Changeling left Arcadia. I didn't especially see agency before to be lost. Shit happens, you react. There is your agency. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Plenty of agency after a Changeling has a Seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T12:57:48-07:00","id":1112289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112232#post1112232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hrm. I quite liked that. Still, hoping Clarity is the same sliding, XP-less scale it was before.<br /> <br /> Still, something that was mentioned on the other thread is that Seeming is still agency-it just wasn't <i>supposed </i>to be, when assigned by your Keeper. An example is a living thunderstorm Elemental who traps her Keeper in a deluge and blows away the walls of his domain. She's an expert disaster relief specialist, now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still a little unsure I understand the new Seemings. <br /> <br /> If I'm understanding correctly, David's Seemings were basically how you forged your Wyrd or what's left of your soul to escape Arcadia. It was litterral and Branding almost. In a way it was like making a pact with an &quot;effort&quot; on the escape. I liked this, True Fae didn't make a seeming or assign a Seeming anymore, the Seeming was how the Changeling escaped (and how it now marks the changeling). With David's approach, I could see changelings with the same Seeming as maybe a little more connected as they all branded themselves in the same way to escape regardless of what their Keeper made them into. <br /> <br /> - for example a Puppet that was forced to dance their way onto stage every night to dance and die for the nightly plays doesn't define the changeling as much as how he escaped by dressing up a companion in his cloathes so that the Keeper wouldn't noticed that he'd been switched. The Darkling, despite still looking like a puppet is still a Darkling and you can see that in the shifting pale color of his wooden skin. <br /> <br /> The new Seeming (again, if I'm understanding correctly), seems to require a lot more. It's now all three. The Gentry picks the Seeming (or Arcadia/The Wyrd does if it happens over time) THEN the Changeling also expresses the Seeming when escaping AND ALSO expresses the Seeming in their post Durance Life. The new Seeming system seems to require a lot to happen and it still doesn't seem to retain the Agency of David's version. What if the Elemental (above) decided to sneak out under the cover of darkness with naught but a whisper? And what if they decide to, instead, be a librarian like they used to when the get out?<br /> <br /> - Examples of this version: A keeper fashions Jamie into a Tin Soldier Wizened, Jamie leaves by fighting a bunch of people, and now she's an activist fighting the good fight. <br /> - A keeper starves some guy for days and eventually he toughens up into an Ogre, he then bulldozes his way through the hedge, now he survives the tough jobs so others don't have to. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I feel like I'm not understanding the new Seemings. I feel like I'm missing something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T13:00:03-07:00","id":1112290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112192#post1112192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Kiths encompass multiple seemings. Each kith has example interpretations for at least two seemings. Here's an example:</div> </div> </div> </div> Interesting, so you can still be any kith/seeming combo, with limited examples for each Kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T13:22:23-07:00","id":1112303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112289#post1112289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the Elemental (above) decided to sneak out under the cover of darkness with naught but a whisper? And what if they decide to, instead, be a librarian like they used to when the get out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are all valid character choices.<br /> <br /> In functional scheme of the game, seemings are about fairy tale archetypes, and they're about the tools a newly-escaped changeling starts with. The storm elemental who decides to escape by disguising herself as a clear night and drifting gently over her Keeper's gates into the Hedge is a supported choice. Changelings are all about defying what others try to make them, and it's as legitimate to subvert or abandon the role your Keeper put you in as it is to turn that role into a weapon against them.<br /> <br /> A changeling can also make any choice she wants in the mortal world. I told the story of the elemental who embodies the persistence of nature, and an elemental seeming would give her tools to pursue that, but she could choose another route.<br /> <br /> As a player, you can choose seeming based on what your character's Keeper made him, based on how he defied or subverted that, or based on what abilities you want him to start with in those early, tough days of coping with the world.<br /> <br /> From an IC perspective, &quot;seeming&quot; is a way escaped changelings talk about a variety of elements of form, powers, and personality. There's no blood test that tells you whether Jack Straw of the Autumn Court is a Wizened for his secret knowledge of the ways of crows or a Darkling for the secrets the birds tell him and which he keeps close to his heart.<br /> <br /> So while we, as designers, handle seeming by drawing a strong archetype and filling it with themed options, building a character who takes some of those options and defies others is entirely intended.<br /> <br /> From both perspectives, there are more potential seemings than the core six, and I view &quot;build your own seeming&quot; as a likely subject for a player's guide chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T13:26:02-07:00","id":1112307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112289#post1112289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the Elemental (above) decided to sneak out under the cover of darkness with naught but a whisper? And what if they decide to, instead, be a librarian like they used to when the get out?</div> </div> </div> </div>If that Elemental came from that place and still wound up fashioned into a castle-guarding thunderstorm, sneaking out is not likely to have been a personal strength that was helped by their transformation. It can be done, but example characters are not the place to show that off.<br /> <br /> Something I like about <i>both</i> presented versions of 2e that was somewhat absent in 1e is the sense that what you were before the Durance had an actual influence on what you became through it \u2014 I can do without seeing the arbitrary darlings of the white room privileged over fairy-tale monsters with a thematic continuity to them. We don't need more characters whose Durance started with a random kidnapping and ended unremarkably, and there's a world of difference between owning your role and ignoring it entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T13:30:06-07:00","id":1112310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112307#post1112307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can do without seeing the arbitrary darlings of the white room privileged over fairy-tale monsters with a thematic continuity to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this line. And that's a good point, though in many games it seems to kind of expect you to either keep in mind who your character was before their Embrace/First Change/Awakening/Durance and so forth, or just drop kick it to the side.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T13:32:44-07:00","id":1112312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112303#post1112303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In functional scheme of the game, seemings are about fairy tale archetypes, and they're about the tools a newly-escaped changeling starts with. The storm elemental who decides to escape by disguising herself as a clear night and drifting gently over her Keeper's gates into the Hedge is a supported choice. Changelings are all about defying what others try to make them, and it's as legitimate to subvert or abandon the role your Keeper put you in as it is to turn that role into a weapon against them.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> As a player, you can choose seeming based on what your character's Keeper made him, based on how he defied or subverted that, or based on what abilities you want him to start with in those early, tough days of coping with the world.<br /> <br /> From an IC perspective, &quot;seeming&quot; is a way escaped changelings talk about a variety of elements of form, powers, and personality. There's no blood test that tells you whether Jack Straw of the Autumn Court is a Wizened for his secret knowledge of the ways of crows or a Darkling for the secrets the birds tell him and which he keeps close to his heart.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> From both perspectives, there are more potential seemings than the core six, and I view &quot;build your own seeming&quot; as a likely subject for a player's guide chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the reply ^.^ I think I understand it now and it makes sense. I think I like it this way as well ^.^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T14:20:23-07:00","id":1112337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112289#post1112289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm still a little unsure I understand the new Seemings.<br /> <br /> If I'm understanding correctly, David's Seemings were basically how you forged your Wyrd or what's left of your soul to escape Arcadia. It was litterral and Branding almost. In a way it was like making a pact with an &quot;effort&quot; on the escape. I liked this, True Fae didn't make a seeming or assign a Seeming anymore, the Seeming was how the Changeling escaped (and how it now marks the changeling). With David's approach, I could see changelings with the same Seeming as maybe a little more connected as they all branded themselves in the same way to escape regardless of what their Keeper made them into.<br /> <br /> - for example a Puppet that was forced to dance their way onto stage every night to dance and die for the nightly plays doesn't define the changeling as much as how he escaped by dressing up a companion in his cloathes so that the Keeper wouldn't noticed that he'd been switched. The Darkling, despite still looking like a puppet is still a Darkling and you can see that in the shifting pale color of his wooden skin.<br /> <br /> The new Seeming (again, if I'm understanding correctly), seems to require a lot more. It's now all three. The Gentry picks the Seeming (or Arcadia/The Wyrd does if it happens over time) THEN the Changeling also expresses the Seeming when escaping AND ALSO expresses the Seeming in their post Durance Life. The new Seeming system seems to require a lot to happen and it still doesn't seem to retain the Agency of David's version. What if the Elemental (above) decided to sneak out under the cover of darkness with naught but a whisper? And what if they decide to, instead, be a librarian like they used to when the get out?<br /> <br /> - Examples of this version: A keeper fashions Jamie into a Tin Soldier Wizened, Jamie leaves by fighting a bunch of people, and now she's an activist fighting the good fight.<br /> - A keeper starves some guy for days and eventually he toughens up into an Ogre, he then bulldozes his way through the hedge, now he survives the tough jobs so others don't have to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I feel like I'm not understanding the new Seemings. I feel like I'm missing something.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Last time I checked, your Kith is the role your Keeper forced you to play, and your Seeming is the method in which you broke free of their control. You are still bound to your Kith, but your Seeming allows you to shape that Kith according to your own personality.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Runnerswift may look and act completely different from other Runnerswifts, depending on if it is an Ogre, Fairest, Darkling, Beast, Wizened, Elemental or Grimm.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is different from 1E in which all Runnerswift were Beasts, all Firehearts were Elementals, all Blood Brutes were Ogres, est. The rules of 2E allow for much broader customization, which I think is rather awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T15:09:56-07:00","id":1112366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112337#post1112337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Last time I checked, your Kith is the role your Keeper forced you to play, and your Seeming is the method in which you broke free of their control. You are still bound to your Kith, but your Seeming allows you to shape that Kith according to your own personality.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Runnerswift may look and act completely different from other Runnerswifts, depending on if it is an Ogre, Fairest, Darkling, Beast, Wizened, Elemental or Grimm.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is different from 1E in which all Runnerswift were Beasts, all Firehearts were Elementals, all Blood Brutes were Ogres, est. The rules of 2E allow for much broader customization, which I think is rather awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You may want to read more of this thread and the True Fae Blog post. There are some changes to the presentations of Seemings between the previous 2e spoilers and the current 2e version that are being discussed here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":". 07-06-2017, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T23:42:02-07:00","id":1112527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112366#post1112366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may want to read more of this thread and the True Fae Blog post. There are some changes to the presentations of Seemings between the previous 2e spoilers and the current 2e version that are being discussed here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it hasn't changed that much, case in point being...\\<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">His patients ended up with any seeming, depending on what kinds of tortures he devised and how they managed to endure them.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Also, the comments I've read further confirm that Seeming is <i>still </i>shaped by the changeling's means of escape. But it looks like they interjected a bit of 1E by highlighting that is inflicted (in part) by the Gentry. I find that it makes sense, though. You take the scars inflicted on you and use it as your way to break free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T23:56:50-07:00","id":1112530,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a>, I have only one question on new 2E Seemings - <b>Are Seemings physically branding characters like before?</b> I.E. If I choose Wizened character, will it need to have added tubes or needles - like some fairy tale cyborg - or that character can be just smaller or more 'saged', with wrinkles, from endless trying doing their Kiths job?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-07-2017, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T00:08:15-07:00","id":1112535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112530#post1112530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I.E. If I choose Wizined character, will it need to have added tubes or needeles - like some fairy tale cyborg - or that character can be just smaller or more 'saged', with wrinkless, from endless trying doing their Kiths job?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyrd, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/706070-new-wizened-inspiration-characters?p=708272#post708272\">we did the &quot;fairy tale cyborg&quot; conversation over a year ago</a>. &quot;Ditch-digger with hands like shovels&quot; and &quot;jeweler with eyes like magnifying glasses&quot; don't necessitate literal incorporation of objects into your mien.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T00:15:43-07:00","id":1112540,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a> <br /> <br /> I also wanted to ask about the mechanics for Regalia. Contracts were initially presented as having various Seeming-based Clauses. Is this retained under the Regalia system? Or is it replaced?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T05:14:41-07:00","id":1112608,"title":"","content":"So. Changes to Seeming. After reading around, it seems a lot like its more of a thematic shift than a mechanical one. Back when Goblin Contracts were released, I talked about how the six Regalia seemed to line up with the six Seeming affinities. So, that really just leaves Seeming Blessing, Seeming Curse and Clarity bumps/breaking points as the method of making a Seeming. <br /> <br /> If you want to make a Seeming around the role of being an artist, for instance (just go with it for now, please), you'd start by assigning what the Seeming is mentally affected by (+Clarity for art that expresses who someone is, Clarity BP for making art that someone else is pushing them to do), some archetype bonuses / Curses (No penalties when making art, All the penalties for purely functional, non-artistic crafting), and quite possibly an affinity Regalia, we'll say Shield for now. <br /> <br /> And you're pretty much done. Most writeups could use a bit more meat, but this is the bare bones that you need for playing.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T07:18:16-07:00","id":1112660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112540#post1112540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> <br /> <br /> I also wanted to ask about the mechanics for Regalia. Contracts were initially presented as having various Seeming-based Clauses. Is this retained under the Regalia system? Or is it replaced?</div> </div> </div> </div> She has said previously that Arcadian contracts will still having Seeming Affinities, although all of the contracts in a particular regalia will have at least one type of Seeming Affinity in common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T08:33:39-07:00","id":1112697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112527#post1112527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it hasn't changed that much, case in point being...\\<br /> <br /> [/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]<br /> <br /> Also, the comments I've read further confirm that Seeming is <i>still </i>shaped by the changeling's means of escape. But it looks like they interjected a bit of 1E by highlighting that is inflicted (in part) by the Gentry. I find that it makes sense, though. You take the scars inflicted on you and use it as your way to break free.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yeah, I agree. After all that Rose has clarified it is definitely only a slight change. That's why I said the 'presentation' had changed rather than the true meat of it. I was mostly just pointing out that Nyrufa's comment seemed to be missing the context of those latest spoilers and was just describing the differences between 1e and David's previous spoilered material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T09:11:26-07:00","id":1112722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112697#post1112697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh yeah, I agree. After all that Rose has clarified it is definitely only a slight change. That's why I said the 'presentation' had changed rather than the true meat of it. I was mostly just pointing out that Nyrufa's comment seemed to be missing the context of those latest spoilers and was just describing the differences between 1e and David's previous spoilered material.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think she just added some extra flexibility to it. <br /> <br /> Anyways did anyone else notice that Huntsmen have livery now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T09:57:38-07:00","id":1112758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112527#post1112527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the comments I've read further confirm that Seeming is <i>still </i>shaped by the changeling's means of escape. But it looks like they interjected a bit of 1E by highlighting that is inflicted (in part) by the Gentry. I find that it makes sense, though. You take the scars inflicted on you and use it as your way to break free.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems mostly now that there isn't any one way that for sure creates a Seeming. Anything really can make a Seeming. Seemings are now more just loose classifications or fae stereotypes/roles that a changeling considers themselves or is considered whether from how they escaped, what role their Keeper forced them into, or how they cope on the outside (among likely others). It's now a little more broad rather than Matter of fact. <br /> <br /> I have some questions to the implications of this. Seemings (possibly used to) have mechanical effects on the character like additions to the Mein and Benefits/Curses that befit that Seeming. These were mechanical and therefore the seeming really meant something. If these mechanical portions are still tied to a Seeming and Seeming is now more a loose set of categories how do the Seeming mechanics happen? Does the Wyrd latch onto an individual Lost when they consider themselves a certain Seeming?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112530#post1112530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a>, I have only one question on new 2E Seemings - <b>Are Seemings physically branding characters like before?</b> I.E. If I choose Wizened character, will it need to have added tubes or needles - like some fairy tale cyborg - or that character can be just smaller or more 'saged', with wrinkles, from endless trying doing their Kiths job?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this too. Since Seemings are more a thematic grouping, do they still have the mechanics associated?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T10:07:28-07:00","id":1112764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112527#post1112527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it hasn't changed that much, case in point being...\\<br /> <br /> [/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]<br /> <br /> Also, the comments I've read further confirm that Seeming is <i>still </i>shaped by the changeling's means of escape. But it looks like they interjected a bit of 1E by highlighting that is inflicted (in part) by the Gentry. I find that it makes sense, though. You take the scars inflicted on you and use it as your way to break free.</div> </div> </div> </div> Kind of reminds me of Princess Leia strangling Jabba the Hut with her own chains. <br /> <br /> I guess she would have the BDSM Seeming ;p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T11:26:11-07:00","id":1112805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112764#post1112764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kind of reminds me of Princess Leia strangling Jabba the Hut with her own chains.<br /> <br /> I guess she would have the BDSM Seeming ;p</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I want to say... Darkling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T12:05:38-07:00","id":1112825,"title":"","content":"Can someone explain Regalia to me? I'm having a hard time understanding them from what I've read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T12:16:07-07:00","id":1112831,"title":"","content":"So it sounds like Seemings and Clarity are both being re-written? That's too bad, as those were the two deal making or breaking points for me. Seems like other folks are happy with the changes, so I hope thins Changeling is the best it can be for those who are liking the new direction. Personally though, it looks like this Changeling won't be for me. At least I know now. Best of luck, everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T12:27:19-07:00","id":1112837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112825#post1112825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone explain Regalia to me? I'm having a hard time understanding them from what I've read.</div> </div> </div> </div>For changelings, a Regalia is a thematic category of Arcadian Contracts, and each seeming has a natural affinity for one of them; then you choose a second favored Regalia at character creation. The six Regalia are: Crown, Jewels, Mirror, Shield, Steed, and Sword.<br /> <br /> For the Gentry, a Regalia is that, but also a part of their vast panoply. The Arcadian Contracts all come from Fae pacts with the themes as a whole--so you can use Steed Contracts because the True Fae, at some point, made a pact with the concepts of movement and time and space. The more powerful a Fae is, the more of those pacts it has the right to draw on. Because their power is so much more all-encompassing, the price they pay is also steeper: they must manifest a physical representation of each Regalia they have access to and protect it, lest it be used against them. This is why the Regalia are named after items of regal panoply, because that's how the Gentry perceive them--these are both literally and figuratively the Regalia with which they adorn themselves as lords of Faerie. (They don't all have to look like literal crowns and swords, though. They can be other kinds of objects that fit the same themes.)<br /> <br /> Court Contracts and Goblin Contracts don't have Regalia because they didn't come from the True Fae, and therefore they don't inherit that aspect of fae power.<br /> <br /> I hope I helped clear it up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T12:40:30-07:00","id":1112854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112805#post1112805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I want to say... Darkling?</div> </div> </div> </div> Orger probably, escape by violence, I love Princess Leia would be an Orger!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T12:52:59-07:00","id":1112860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112831#post1112831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it sounds like Seemings and Clarity are both being re-written? That's too bad, as those were the two deal making or breaking points for me. Seems like other folks are happy with the changes, so I hope thins Changeling is the best it can be for those who are liking the new direction. Personally though, it looks like this Changeling won't be for me. At least I know now. Best of luck, everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div> What is the change to Clarity?<br /> <br /> As for Seeming and Kiths, the change seems to be minor, more flexiblity. Don't get me wrong, I wasn't happy either, but the changes aren't so major as to be a deal breaker for me, I still want the kickstarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 07-07-2017, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T12:59:14-07:00","id":1112866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112837#post1112837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For changelings, a Regalia is a thematic category of Arcadian Contracts, and each seeming has a natural affinity for one of them; then you choose a second favored Regalia at character creation. The six Regalia are: Crown, Jewels, Mirror, Shield, Steed, and Sword.<br /> <br /> For the Gentry, a Regalia is that, but also a part of their vast panoply. The Arcadian Contracts all come from Fae pacts with the themes as a whole--so you can use Steed Contracts because the True Fae, at some point, made a pact with the concepts of movement and time and space. The more powerful a Fae is, the more of those pacts it has the right to draw on. Because their power is so much more all-encompassing, the price they pay is also steeper: they must manifest a physical representation of each Regalia they have access to and protect it, lest it be used against them. This is why the Regalia are named after items of regal panoply, because that's how the Gentry perceive them--these are both literally and figuratively the Regalia with which they adorn themselves as lords of Faerie. (They don't all have to look like literal crowns and swords, though. They can be other kinds of objects that fit the same themes.)<br /> <br /> Court Contracts and Goblin Contracts don't have Regalia because they didn't come from the True Fae, and therefore they don't inherit that aspect of fae power.<br /> <br /> I hope I helped clear it up!</div> </div> </div> </div> I had assumed that Steed would be more about animals and linked to Beasts, but if Steed are about Movement, Time, and Space, I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> My guess would have been Crown = Fairest, Jewel = Elemental, Mirror = Darkling, Shield = Wizened, Sword = Orger, Steed = Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T13:09:15-07:00","id":1112874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112831#post1112831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it sounds like Seemings and Clarity are both being re-written? That's too bad, as those were the two deal making or breaking points for me. Seems like other folks are happy with the changes, so I hope thins Changeling is the best it can be for those who are liking the new direction. Personally though, it looks like this Changeling won't be for me. At least I know now. Best of luck, everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say happy so much as <i>pacified</i>. It's not as bad as I feared (like 1st ed with more steps), but it's not as great as David's version was. It still feels like a step back but to so far as going back to 1st Ed. So i'm, <i>Pacified</i>.<br /> <br /> Like, at least they're thematic only so any explanation for a Seeming being what it is is valid. Still, I personally loved and fell in love with David's version where you litterrally ahd to mark your soul to escape creating a Seeming on your Mein. It was visceral almost and deeply personal and the mechanics really backed that up. Seemings meant a huge amount in that version.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112860#post1112860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is the change to Clarity?<br /> <br /> As for Seeming and Kiths, the change seems to be minor, more flexibility. Don't get me wrong, I wasn't happy either, but the changes are so major as to be a deal breaker for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite a deal breaker for me. Just much disappoint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112837#post1112837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope I helped clear it up!</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually helped a lot! I think I really get it for the True Fae Regalia.<br /> <br /> A little unsure on Changeling Regalia Contracts. Do the replace the general contracts from 1st Ed? And if so are there more than those 6?<br /> <br /> Like I remember 1st Ed had:<br /> - General Contracts: contracts that could be taken by anyone (like the contract of shadows or the contracts of chance)<br /> - Seeming Contracts: Contracts that were tied to Seemings (like the Contracts of elements or the Contracts of Tooth and Nail)<br /> - Court Contracts: Contracts (around 3 by the end) that were tied to a Court (like fear or sorrow)<br /> - Goblin Contracts: One-clause contracts with a specific dot rating that could be bought from Markets and were one-off uses.<br /> <br /> So If I'm getting this correctly, 2nd Ed is:<br /> - Regalia contracts: one of 6 Contracts that tie back to the True Fae deals<br /> - goblin Contracts: (do these still work the same way?)<br /> - Court Contracts: Contracts a court strikes with an emotion?<br /> <br /> Am I getting that correctly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T13:21:42-07:00","id":1112883,"title":"","content":"Regalia aren't particular contracts, they are grouping of contracts.<br /> <br /> Like Arcadian Contracts (what they call universal/general contracts now) have a least six groupings of contracts, so Sword Regalia might Contracts A, B, and C, ect...., all related to the broad themes of the Sword Regalia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T13:40:29-07:00","id":1112897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112854#post1112854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Orger probably, escape by violence, I love Princess Leia would be an Orger!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except it wasn't her own violence. She waited until somebody came to rescue her before she started to fight back.<br /> <br /> Also, she pretty much lead the empire straight to the door step of the rebel base once she had the top secret files. She could have transmitted them directly to the rebels and kept their location a secret, but decided to put the entire organization in jeopardy so that she could evade capture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T15:31:18-07:00","id":1112962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112860#post1112860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is the change to Clarity?</div> </div> </div> </div>From Rose's quote in the other thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112118#post1112118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The True Fae's lack of Clarity says some interesting things about them. Clarity, in second edition, is about owning your own perceptions, knowing your own truth. As a changeling, you always see both the mortal and faerie worlds. The powers of both those worlds tell you that their &quot;side&quot; is the only one that matters, the only one that's real, and you say &quot;no, I know what I see and where I've been, I know who I am.&quot;<br /> <br /> The True Fae don't have that. The world-shaping power of their own will blinds them to realities they don't control, that aren't part of their web of agreements and illusions. Rather than knowing their own truth, they force their whims to act like truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a huge change, but another slight shift in emphasis compared to the previously spoiled Clarity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112860#post1112860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Seeming and Kiths, the change seems to be minor, more flexiblity. Don't get me wrong, I wasn't happy either, but the changes aren't so major as to be a deal breaker for me, I still want the kickstarter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, not a huge change. Not a deal breaker on its own. The thing is, between Clarity and Seemings both getting a shift in emphasis, I would be very surprised if Blessings, Curses, Breaking Points, and Acuity survive these changes intact. And it was that system that made Changeling for me. I wasn't much of a Changeling girl in 1e, but that system sold me on it, and would have made it my favorite CofD game. If it's gone, I'm not really interested any more. Which is fine, honestly; I'm always the first to preach that not every game line can be for everyone. I'm a little disappointed that Changeling 2 isn't going to be for me, since it had been looking like it <i>really</i> would be, but at this point I'm just glad to know so I can refocus my energy on the other awesome gamelines CofD has to offer. I tuly hope the game turns out great for those who it is for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-07-2017, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T18:41:56-07:00","id":1113037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112860#post1112860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Seeming and Kiths, the change seems to be minor, more flexiblity. Don't get me wrong, I wasn't happy either, but the changes aren't so major as to be a deal breaker for me, I still want the kickstarter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Seemings were &quot;super thematic things which resonanted with my experience of pain and suffering and mental illness and really tied into the wyrd&quot; and are now &quot;Whatever you want, we really don't give it any specific flavour anymore&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T19:11:51-07:00","id":1113049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1113037#post1113037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and are now &quot;Whatever you want, we really don't give it any specific flavour anymore&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait, what? I'm confused now!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T19:23:40-07:00","id":1113056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1113049#post1113049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wait, what? I'm confused now!</div> </div> </div> </div>We've been informed by Rose that seemings are decided on by &quot;X, or y, or z, or k, or w... etc.&quot;<br /> <br /> When seeming can represent any one thing from such a massive list it doesn't really have much flavour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T22:35:41-07:00","id":1113118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1113056#post1113056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've been informed by Rose that seemings are decided on by &quot;X, or y, or z, or k, or w... etc.&quot;<br /> <br /> When seeming can represent any one thing from such a massive list it doesn't really have much flavour.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>So, in other words:</b> an Ogre doesn't necessarily have to be about violence and brutishness, or a Fairest about charisma and leadership?<br /> <br /> <br /> I feel like a more in depth explanation would be necessary to help understand what makes the Seemings different from each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T22:58:54-07:00","id":1113127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1113118#post1113118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>So, in other words:</b> an Ogre doesn't necessarily have to be about violence and brutishness, or a Fairest about charisma and leadership?<br /> <br /> <br /> I feel like a more in depth explanation would be necessary to help understand what makes the Seemings different from each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it sounds more like how a changeling acquires their Seeming could be very several reasons instead of just one and only one cause.<br /> <br /> To use your example it: no, Ogres are still about violence and brutishness and Fairest are still about charisma and leadership. HOW the Ogre acquired the violence and brutishness and the Fairest with charisma and leadership is not as rigorously defined.<br /> <br /> I'm left with the impression that someone on the development team liked the 1e version of Seemings enough to want to keep them for 2e...but at the same time didn't want to completely throw out Hill's version of Seemings either so now we have both simultaneously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 07-08-2017, 02:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T23:37:46-07:00","id":1113132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1113118#post1113118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>So, in other words:</b> an Ogre doesn't necessarily have to be about violence and brutishness, or a Fairest about charisma and leadership?</div> </div> </div> </div>A changeling could be an ogre if they were made into a warrior by their keeper, if they were being brutish during their durance, if they fought their way out of their durance, if there were a noble in their durance and they ended up subverting it by being really trashy, or &quot;if you just wanted the ogre abilities&quot;.<br /> <br /> Seeming as described represents &quot;something&quot;, but the amount of somethings that are available is too large for me to actually see as having any meaning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 07-08-2017, 02:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T23:48:31-07:00","id":1113135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1113132#post1113132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A changeling could be an ogre if they were made into a warrior by their keeper, if they were being brutish during their durance, if they fought their way out of their durance, if there were a noble in their durance and they ended up subverting it by being really trashy, <b>or &quot;if you just wanted the ogre abilities&quot;.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Hey Milo?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>As a player, you can choose seeming</b> based on what your character's Keeper made him, based on how he defied or subverted that, or<b> based on what abilities you want him to start with in those early, tough days of coping with the world.</b> </div> </div> </div>Let's not be <i>incredibly terribly uncharitable </i>by characterizing the above &quot;you made this character as this seeming because the abilities of that seeming were what you wanted in their toolkit close to hand at the beginning of their narrative in the game&quot; as &quot;you just wanted the powers.&quot; It benefits nothing and nobody to do this thing. A character who spends most of their running story with access to the power of flight develops differently than a character who picks up that ability after years of being able to talk to birds and leash thunderstorms even if both end up with functionally identical lists of abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T00:26:21-07:00","id":1113137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1113127#post1113127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it sounds more like how a changeling acquires their Seeming could be very several reasons instead of just one and only one cause.<br /> <br /> To use your example it: no, Ogres are still about violence and brutishness and Fairest are still about charisma and leadership. HOW the Ogre acquired the violence and brutishness and the Fairest with charisma and leadership is not as rigorously defined.<br /> <br /> I'm left with the impression that someone on the development team liked the 1e version of Seemings enough to want to keep them for 2e...but at the same time didn't want to completely throw out Hill's version of Seemings either so now we have both simultaneously.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is the case - I'm more than content. I liked that Hill's Seemings were more open than 1E, but I <i>really hated</i> that all Fairest must be about freeing slaves, or all Darklings are damn backstabbers, everyone of them. If I can make Fairest 'princess' non-black&amp;white changeling character that was risen by her Keeper to be 'Fairest of them All' - and that character is lost in the deep when in Ironside, trying to understand her Keeper <i>did </i>bad thing by kidnapping her - it's FINALLY the <b>CtL</b> I loved in 1E gameline.<br /> <br /> Having Seeming forced by Keeper is ALSO tragic story, you know...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-08-2017, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T00:57:23-07:00","id":1113143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1113135#post1113135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not be <i>incredibly terribly uncharitable </i>by characterizing the above &quot;you made this character as this seeming because the abilities of that seeming were what you wanted in their toolkit close to hand at the beginning of their narrative in the game&quot; as &quot;you just wanted the powers.&quot; It benefits nothing and nobody to do this thing. A character who spends most of their running story with access to the power of flight develops differently than a character who picks up that ability after years of being able to talk to birds and leash thunderstorms even if both end up with functionally identical lists of abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>My issue with that is that is has nothing to do with in-verse justification, meaning you don't need an actual reason for the character to have the seeming. It wasn't intended to be a negative judgement on people who use take that &quot;justification&quot;, I'm sure there will be people who benefit from being able to just take a seeming because they wanted their character a certain way. <br /> <br /> I was specifically talking about how there are far too many &quot;in-setting justifications&quot; for having a certain seeming, and one is specifically &quot;you don't need an actual reason&quot;. Perhaps I should have put more emphasis on the &quot;in-setting&quot; part?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 07-08-2017, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T03:13:21-07:00","id":1113170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1113037#post1113037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except Seemings were &quot;super thematic things which resonanted with my experience of pain and suffering and mental illness and really tied into the wyrd&quot; and are now &quot;Whatever you want, we really don't give it any specific flavour anymore&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if I have some misgivings on what we know about Seemings right now, which is not exactly the same as information presented in the upcoming text of the books, this strikes me as horribly uncharitable. Seeming is now more a matter of &quot;face&quot;-imposed on you at first, and yet can be warped and changed into a tool of identity expression. It literally becomes a battleground for the control over self-perception, which is certainly not a bad way of going about the concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T03:52:23-07:00","id":1113173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112962#post1112962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From Rose's quote in the other thread:<br /> <br /> <br /> Not a huge change, but another slight shift in emphasis compared to the previously spoiled Clarity.<br /> <br /> <br /> Again, not a huge change. Not a deal breaker on its own. The thing is, between Clarity and Seemings both getting a shift in emphasis, I would be very surprised if Blessings, Curses, Breaking Points, and Acuity survive these changes intact. And it was that system that made Changeling for me. I wasn't much of a Changeling girl in 1e, but that system sold me on it, and would have made it my favorite CofD game. If it's gone, I'm not really interested any more. Which is fine, honestly; I'm always the first to preach that not every game line can be for everyone. I'm a little disappointed that Changeling 2 isn't going to be for me, since it had been looking like it <i>really</i> would be, but at this point I'm just glad to know so I can refocus my energy on the other awesome gamelines CofD has to offer. I tuly hope the game turns out great for those who it is for.</div> </div> </div> </div> Perhaps wait for more details, I'm betting Acuity is still a thing, the mechanic is really cool, too cool to dump.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T03:55:13-07:00","id":1113175,"title":"","content":"No risk without reward.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Clarity, I know nothing. No, that's not a pun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T08:14:04-07:00","id":1113248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1113173#post1113173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps wait for more details, I'm betting Acuity is still a thing, the mechanic is really cool, too cool to dump.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not Acuity my interest hinges on, but the interplay between Acuity, Breaking Points, and Seeming Blessings and Curses. And if I'm wrong and they're keeping those mechanics the same while changing the narrative connected to them, I can only wonder why. Those mechanics expressed the concepts that they represented, in many ways better than the narrative even did. Transplanting those mechanics onto a different narrative would just be... a very strange choice. It wouldn't be a deal breaking one at that point, but it would be a very confusing one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T08:41:26-07:00","id":1113261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1113143#post1113143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was specifically talking about how there are far too many &quot;in-setting justifications&quot; for having a certain seeming, and one is specifically &quot;you don't need an actual reason&quot;. Perhaps I should have put more emphasis on the &quot;in-setting&quot; part?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're looking to a list of player-as-character-author justifications and expecting it to contain player-as-character-actor justifications <i>and also still ignoring that the one you're taking specific issue with is not what you are claiming it to be</i>.<br /> <br /> The options aren't &quot;your character was made into an Ogre, your character became an Ogre as they broke free from their Keeper, your character became an Ogre Because Reasons,&quot; they're &quot;you want to play someone who was made into an Ogre by what they escaped, you want to play someone who made themselves into an Ogre to escape, you want to play someone whose escape made them into an Ogre.&quot;<br /> <br /> None of these are more &quot;in-setting&quot; justification than the other, because they are there to address the intent of the character's creator in pursuing that seeming's thematic niche rather than the in-character process of picking up that seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T11:52:11-07:00","id":1113308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1113248#post1113248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not Acuity my interest hinges on, but the interplay between Acuity, Breaking Points, and Seeming Blessings and Curses. And if I'm wrong and they're keeping those mechanics the same while changing the narrative connected to them, I can only wonder why. Those mechanics expressed the concepts that they represented, in many ways better than the narrative even did. Transplanting those mechanics onto a different narrative would just be... a very strange choice. It wouldn't be a deal breaking one at that point, but it would be a very confusing one.</div> </div> </div> </div> Until we see the current state of the mechanics for clairity &amp; seemings no way to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T15:56:36-07:00","id":1113915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1113248#post1113248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not Acuity my interest hinges on, but the interplay between Acuity, Breaking Points, and Seeming Blessings and Curses. And if I'm wrong and they're keeping those mechanics the same while changing the narrative connected to them, I can only wonder why. Those mechanics expressed the concepts that they represented, in many ways better than the narrative even did. Transplanting those mechanics onto a different narrative would just be... a very strange choice. It wouldn't be a deal breaking one at that point, but it would be a very confusing one.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the narrative that the 1.5 Clarity (what David Hill previewed before) supports, and what's the narrative that the 2.0 Clarity (what's being implied with Rose Bailey's preview that is not about Clarity)?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To the changes on Seeming myself: As someone who was impressed by how every time a word in the ChroD games meant something significant rather than just stapling cool-looking words, I now look at what the word <i>seeming </i>means.<br /> <br /> You are seemingly an animal, because your captor chained and whipped you like one, but now you can be more than what your captor forced you to be and the chains you already broke.<br /> <br /> You are seemingly a brute, because you chose to be so in the face of hardship, but now that you are no longer pushed to the brinks you can be more than what you had to be.<br /> <br /> You are seemingly a prince, because you seized leadership and make the grand escape, but now you have a whole new life of new choices that need not be defined by a single choice in your life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T16:45:08-07:00","id":1113940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1113915#post1113915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the narrative that the 1.5 Clarity (what David Hill previewed before) supports, and what's the narrative that the 2.0 Clarity (what's being implied with Rose Bailey's preview that is not about Clarity)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The previous system reflected reactions to and mechanics for coping trauma in the mechanics for Seeming Blessings and Curses, post-traumatic stress triggers in Clarity Breaking Points, and the Acuity Condition reflected the need to face one's trauma in order to overcome it. See my previous post where I quoted Rose saying what Clarity represents in 2e for what the new version of Clarity represents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T17:47:11-07:00","id":1113960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1113940#post1113940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The previous system reflected reactions to and mechanics for coping trauma in the mechanics for Seeming Blessings and Curses, post-traumatic stress triggers in Clarity Breaking Points, and the Acuity Condition reflected the need to face one's trauma in order to overcome it. See my previous post where I quoted Rose saying what Clarity represents in 2e for what the new version of Clarity represents.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, missed that post. I was reading through this thread a bit too quickly, it seems.<br /> <br /> Still... is the narrative of facing one's trauma to overcome it mutually exclusive with that of knowing your own truth? Maybe it's just me, but I didn't feel the two were so different. Probably has to do with how I enjoyed the Persona series, where facing your own traumas was equal to understanding who you truly are and who you are not. And how the metaphor of the True Fae as the ultimate escapists who can't stand to face the harsh iron-cold reality and flee in their own desires, thereby lacking Clarity in both the face-your-scars and know-who-you-are senses rang so clear to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T21:39:05-07:00","id":1114043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1113960#post1113960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, missed that post. I was reading through this thread a bit too quickly, it seems.<br /> <br /> Still... is the narrative of facing one's trauma to overcome it mutually exclusive with that of knowing your own truth? Maybe it's just me, but I didn't feel the two were so different. Probably has to do with how I enjoyed the Persona series, where facing your own traumas was equal to understanding who you truly are and who you are not. And how the metaphor of the True Fae as the ultimate escapists who can't stand to face the harsh iron-cold reality and flee in their own desires, thereby lacking Clarity in both the face-your-scars and know-who-you-are senses rang so clear to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. To be clear, I don't have a problem with Rose's brief summary of 2e Clarity. I was very attached to how the specific mechanics of Seeming Blessings and Curses, Clarity Breaking Points, and Acuity perfectly expressed through the gameplay what David's Clarity was all about. Those mechanics, and the interaction between them, are what won me over on 2e Changeling. If those mechanics remain in the final draft, 2e Changeling will maintain my interest. If not, it won't. I guess we don't have proof positive that those mechanics won't remain in the final draft. But with the subtle shifts in presentation of both Seemings and Clarity, I am no longer holding out hope that they will remain in the final draft. I'd be thrilled if I turn out to be wrong about this, but the signs sure seem to me to be pointing to those mechanics getting changed in a way I won't be happy with.<br /> <br /> This is, by the way, entirely a me thing. I get why it's not a dealbreaking issue for others. And maybe it's silly of me to hold this specific cow so sacred. But that's how it is for me. I'm not trying to convince anyone it should be that way for them too. As I said before, I hope Changeling 2e is the best game it can be for those who are liking the new direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T23:31:06-07:00","id":1114072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1114043#post1114043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure. To be clear, I don't have a problem with Rose's brief summary of 2e Clarity. I was very attached to how the specific mechanics of Seeming Blessings and Curses, Clarity Breaking Points, and Acuity perfectly expressed through the gameplay what David's Clarity was all about. Those mechanics, and the interaction between them, are what won me over on 2e Changeling. If those mechanics remain in the final draft, 2e Changeling will maintain my interest. If not, it won't. I guess we don't have proof positive that those mechanics won't remain in the final draft. But with the subtle shifts in presentation of both Seemings and Clarity, I am no longer holding out hope that they will remain in the final draft. I'd be thrilled if I turn out to be wrong about this, but the signs sure seem to me to be pointing to those mechanics getting changed in a way I won't be happy with.<br /> <br /> This is, by the way, entirely a me thing. I get why it's not a dealbreaking issue for others. And maybe it's silly of me to hold this specific cow so sacred. But that's how it is for me. I'm not trying to convince anyone it should be that way for them too. As I said before, I hope Changeling 2e is the best game it can be for those who are liking the new direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand. A lot of us here agree that gaining Clarity by facing its breaking points was a brilliant idea. I hope that at least the spirit of that mechanic lives in one way or another in the final version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T03:41:10-07:00","id":1114099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1114072#post1114072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand. A lot of us here agree that gaining Clarity by facing its breaking points was a brilliant idea. I hope that at least the spirit of that mechanic lives in one way or another in the final version.</div> </div> </div> </div> Agree, it was inspired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T18:47:10-07:00","id":1115325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1112837#post1112837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For changelings, a Regalia is a thematic category of Arcadian Contracts, and each seeming has a natural affinity for one of them; then you choose a second favored Regalia at character creation. The six Regalia are: Crown, Jewels, Mirror, Shield, Steed, and Sword.<br /> <br /> For the Gentry, a Regalia is that, but also a part of their vast panoply. The Arcadian Contracts all come from Fae pacts with the themes as a whole--so you can use Steed Contracts because the True Fae, at some point, made a pact with the concepts of movement and time and space. The more powerful a Fae is, the more of those pacts it has the right to draw on. Because their power is so much more all-encompassing, the price they pay is also steeper: they must manifest a physical representation of each Regalia they have access to and protect it, lest it be used against them. This is why the Regalia are named after items of regal panoply, because that's how the Gentry perceive them--these are both literally and figuratively the Regalia with which they adorn themselves as lords of Faerie. (They don't all have to look like literal crowns and swords, though. They can be other kinds of objects that fit the same themes.)<br /> <br /> Court Contracts and Goblin Contracts don't have Regalia because they didn't come from the True Fae, and therefore they don't inherit that aspect of fae power.<br /> <br /> I hope I helped clear it up!</div> </div> </div> </div>Do Huntsman have acess to regalia,or do they have different powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T21:29:48-07:00","id":1115379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1115325#post1115325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Huntsman have acess to regalia,or do they have different powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Huntsmen are built like Horrors and hobgoblins, so they use Dread Powers rather than Contracts/Regalia. (And like hobgoblins, they have Wyrd and use Glamour.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T04:22:52-07:00","id":1115462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1115379#post1115379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huntsmen are built like Horrors and hobgoblins, so they use Dread Powers rather than Contracts/Regalia. (And like hobgoblins, they have Wyrd and use Glamour.)</div> </div> </div> </div> Hobgoblin's seemed changed from before when they, used willpower instead of Glamour, interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T06:13:30-07:00","id":1115498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1115379#post1115379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huntsmen are built like Horrors and hobgoblins, so they use Dread Powers rather than Contracts/Regalia. (And like hobgoblins, they have Wyrd and use Glamour.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not too unexpected but it's an interesting way to do it. It seems to say some curious things about them in contrast to Changelings and the Fae.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T10:52:50-07:00","id":1115595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1105463-changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition-what-we-know-so-far?p=1115379#post1115379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huntsmen are built like Horrors and hobgoblins, so they use Dread Powers rather than Contracts/Regalia. (And like hobgoblins, they have Wyrd and use Glamour.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T10:29:39-07:00","id":1116015,"title":"","content":"From Rich's comments on the Dark Eras Kickstarter, it sounds like a Kickstarter for Changeling has been greenlit for later this year. That would certainly explain why the step so s